    "body": "> Why the switch from \"may\"?\r\n\r\nBecause I noticed the build script was changing it anyway. But I guess it should not be.\r\n\r\n> I thought this was normative advice.\r\n\r\nIt is.\r\n\r\n>  It also seems like \"can never\" should be \"must not\"\r\n\r\nYes. I’ve changed it to that.\r\n\r\n>  it's not immediately clear to me what the rationale for that is either\r\n\r\nThe rationale is that these elements can be used as children of the `template` element, separated from the context of `table` tree, and in that different `template` context they never have implicit end tags as far as the parsing behavior/algorithm goes.",
