    "body": "To be more clear, what happens as far as the HTML checker behavior goes is that given this:\r\n\r\n```\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<title>Test</title>\r\n<template>\r\n<td>Foo bar\r\n</template>\r\n```\r\n\r\n…[the checker reports](https://validator.w3.org/nu/?showsource=yes&doc=data%3Atext%2Fhtml%3Bcharset%3Dutf-8%2C%3C%2521DOCTYPE%2520html%3E%250D%250A%3Ctitle%3ETest%3C%252Ftitle%3E%250D%250A%3Ctemplate%3E%250D%250A%3Ctd%3EFoo%2520bar%250D%250A%3C%252Ftemplate%3E):\r\n\r\n> Error: End tag template seen, but there were open elements.\r\n\r\n…because the `td` element never gets closed.\r\n\r\nSame for all the other elements touched in the patch in this PR.\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
