    "body": "> > The rationale is that these elements can be used as children of the template element, separated from the context of table tree, and in that different template context they never have implicit end tags as far as the parsing behavior/algorithm goes.\r\n>\r\n> But maybe they should? Seems annoying to have to write them differently there.\r\n\r\nThat would require all implementors to change their parser code (along with requiring the spec change of course). My sense of things is that in general, implementors are not very interested in making further changes to their parser code, especially for a case such as this that seems like a relatively low priority from any implementor perspective and from the user perspective.\r\n",
