    "body": "> Does `<template><td>...<td>...</td></template>` generate the same error or does that work? \r\n\r\nIt does not generate the same error. It generates no errors.\r\n\r\n> And it would only require changes to code that determines conformance, no?\r\n\r\nNot completely sure what you mean… But I guess you mean in the error-reporting facet of the HTML parser? If so it’s true that the error for `<template><td>Foo bar</template>` case is generated by HTML parser and the checker just passes it on from there.\r\n\r\nBut anyway I wasn’t referring to changes needing to be made to the error reporting in parsers. What I meant about code changes was that parsers would need to be changed to close any open `td` element when the parser encounters a `</template>` end tag.",
