    "body": ">> It does not generate the same error. It generates no errors.\r\n>\r\n> That's already inconsistent with your patch as far as I can tell. Since it says you must never omit it.\r\n\r\nThat patch says:\r\n\r\n> … but must not be omitted if the <code>td</code> element is a child of a <code>template</code> element.\r\n\r\nThat is, “child”, not “descendant”.\r\n\r\n> It's been a while since I looked at the parser, but explicitly closing it would be a no-op here, no? \r\n\r\nOh, I see what you’re getting at. So yeah, I guess so.\r\n\r\n>  It only affects error reporting.\r\n\r\nPerhaps so yeah",
