    "created_at": "2017-05-22T08:43:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-22T08:43:17Z",
    "body": "> Is that bug also present in other implementations?\r\n\r\nNot that I’m aware of but I guess it’s only exposed/observable in an error-reporting parser, right? If so, there are no other error-reporting parsers I’m familiar with so I wouldn’t know how to check\r\n\r\n> Is there a test case in html5lib-tests?\r\n\r\nAgain I’m not sure if it’s testable since it’s just about popping elements off the (internal) stack and the only thing that would manifest if the implementation hasn’t done that is if it also implemented error reporting\r\n",
